<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02376</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>bb8aaf94-7068-4077-a713-3724bf89bdd5</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="dc9f4c75-4245-46cb-94c3-70136138f87a" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ce344af3-e2fc-47e5-89a0-723db7a50b6f" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(\frac94\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(\\frac23\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac49\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac94\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-\\frac23\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For the expressions in questions 1 – 4, choose which number would make the expression a perfect square. Then, choose an equivalent expression in factored form.</para>
      <para>\(x^2+3x\)</para>
      <para>What number can be added to make \(x^2+3x\) a perfect square?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac94\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 and 9.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7824a5c3-ccf6-4a27-a7c5-40d1d790cff9" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(x(x + 3)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x(x + 3)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x(3x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\((x + 3)(x + 3)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(3(x + 1)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2+3x\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x(x + 3)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 and 9.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="997a5371-4e56-4e04-ba7f-782c4c875a94" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="0.09" data-solution-options="[&quot;0.09&quot;, &quot;0.81&quot;, &quot;0.36&quot;, &quot;0.03&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+0.6x\)</para>
      <para> What number can be added to make \(x^2+0.6x\) a perfect square?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 0.09</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 and 9.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c6f1b4c5-0f89-4180-af96-32c5f02c5af2" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(x(x+0.6)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x(x+0.6x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x(x+0.6)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x(0.6x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0.6(x+1)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2+0.6x\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x(x+0.6)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 and 9.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="844310e2-1516-4923-98b9-0f1c94bbd63a" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(\frac{121}{4}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(\\frac{11}{2}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{25}{2}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac52\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{121}{4}\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2-11x\)</para>
      <para>What number can be added to make \(x^2-11x\) a perfect square?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac{121}{4}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 and 9.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="25442b64-c58b-4126-9f4b-9d092761dc32" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(x(x-11)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x(x-11x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x(x-11)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(11(x-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(11x(x-1)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2-11x\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x(x-11)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 and 9.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8cca33a0-b21b-4a19-8aa6-b42f50a7644c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(\frac{25}{16}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(\\frac{25}{4}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{25}{16}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac58\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac68\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2-\frac{5}{2}x\)</para>
      <para> What number can be added to make \(x^2-\frac{5}{2}x\) a perfect square?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac{25}{16}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 and 9.3.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d10954da-8650-4ab4-9d0c-a6a6f2383aa1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(x(x-\frac52)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x(x-\\frac52)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x(x-\\frac{5}{2}x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{5}{2}x(x-1)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{5}{2}(x-1)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which expression is equivalent to \(x^2-\frac{5}{2}x\)?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x(x-\frac52)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.2.2 and 9.2.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="feefda53-6a1a-4443-95d3-5229cbb484a1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(\frac14\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(\\frac14\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac12\\)&quot;, &quot;1&quot;, &quot;0&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What number can be added to make \(x^2+x\) a perfect square?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac14\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.2.2 and 9.2.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c4829eed-28cd-415d-b5d2-48483676a0b1" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(\frac{9}{16}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(\\frac23\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac49\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(\\frac{9}{16}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(-\\frac23\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What number can be added to make \(x^2-\frac{3}{2}x\) a perfect square?  </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(\frac{9}{16}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.2.2 and 9.2.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--7a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e3c26867-40b6-4860-8b80-1204ffe62885" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Noah is solving the equation \(x^2+8x+15=3\). He begins by rewriting the expression on the left in factored form and writes \((x+3)(x+5)=3\). He does not know what to do next. </para>
      <para>Do you think using the factored form is the best way for Noah to solve this equation?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No. Noah should use completing the square.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.3.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--7b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="b310b720-bf24-4fbd-9217-83fe38560355" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x = -2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -6\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = -4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -6\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 4\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Solve the original equation, then choose the<emphasis> two</emphasis> roots.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=-2\) and \(x=-6\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.2.2 and 9.2.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e1a27da5-2ce6-41c4-a658-1abd528f4ea3" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Agree" data-solution-options="[&quot;Agree&quot;, &quot;Disagree&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>An equation and its solutions are given. Solve the equation by completing the square, then choose whether you agree or disagree with the given solutions.</para>
      <para>\(x^2+20x+50=14\). The solutions are \(x=-18\) and \(x=-2\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Agree. The correct solutions are \(x=-18\) and \(x=-2\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.3 and 9.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8d585fd8-2607-4e8f-af9d-0fb10aeea7a4" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Agree" data-solution-options="[&quot;Agree&quot;, &quot;Disagree&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+1.6x=0.36\). The solutions are \(x=-1.8\) and \(x=0.2\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Agree. \(x=-1.8\) and \(x=0.2\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.3 and 9.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3993561c-b0a9-4e42-af8b-5827ff6f7933" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Disagree" data-solution-options="[&quot;Agree&quot;, &quot;Disagree&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2-5x=\frac{11}{4}\). The solutions are \(x=\frac{11}{4}\) and \(x=-12\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Disagree. The correct solutions are \(x=\frac{11}{2}\) and \(x=-\frac12\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.3 and 9.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--9a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e510a689-c1be-4c61-b360-d98732756763" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x = -0.5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 1\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = -0.5\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\( x = 0\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = -1\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Solve each equation, then choose the <emphasis>two</emphasis> roots.</para>
      <para>\(x^2-0.5x=0.5\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=-0.5\) and \(x=1\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 – 9.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--9b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="27b99384-bd9f-47a5-aed0-2d1cbeafe84d" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x = -0.9\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 0.1\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = -0.9\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 0.8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 0.4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 0.1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = 0.81\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+0.8x=0.09\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=-0.9\) and \(x=0.1\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 – 9.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--9c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6c1881a7-7b81-4541-ba80-46f685e9b9ba" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\(x=-\\frac{14}{3}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = \\frac13\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(x = \\frac{28}{3}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x =\\frac{1}{9}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=\\frac{112}{36}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=-\\frac{14}{3}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x = \\frac13\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(x^2+\frac{13}{3}x=\frac{56}{36}\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=-\frac{14}{3}\) and \(x = \frac{1}{3}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.3.2 – 9.3.4. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
</content>
